P0 QP SEMANTIC REVIEW

Current src/qp/registry/replay-v2.ts is not a production verifier yet.

Specific failures in current HEAD:
1. trustedPublicKey is optional. In FULL/CRYPTO when missing:
   checked.signature =3D true // skipped if no trusted key
This is a hard fail-open. FULL must require a configured trust resolver.

2. ReplayInput is caller supplied separately from signed receipt.
claim_id/contract_root/actuality/evidence_root/spec id can be
substituted unless explicitly bound to signed receipt extension.

3. checked.claimBinding exists but is never set/verified.
4. checked.freshness exists but is never checked.
5. checked.gateProgramHash is never actually established.
6. checked.judgeResults is never established.
7. checked.chainLinkage is never established.
8. receiptHash is marked true by comment, not comparison.
9. stateAfterRoot is explicitly "" =E2=80=94 transition program not wired.
10. no authority verification.
11. provenance_policy_hash / independence_policy_hash are not enforced.
12. empty evidence is declared integrity=3Dtrue regardless of spec requirem=
ents.
13. evidence root is recomputed from e.id if present, so
attacker-controlled IDs can stand in for evidence bytes.
14. judge/gate functions are still in-process JS objects whose
bundle_hash can merely be claimed.

REPLACE WITH Replay V3.

Inputs:
  signedReceiptBytes
  privateEvidenceBundle (optional; supplied only to authorized verifier)
  TrustPolicy
  FrozenRegistry

Algorithm:
A. parse raw receipt using upstream Obsigna preserve-unknown-fields/raw ver=
ifier
B. schema validate Agent Receipt + pmail QP extension
C. resolve trusted signer independently
D. upstream Obsigna crypto + chain verification
E. read QP fields ONLY from signed receipt
F. resolve ProofSpec by (spec_id, version, contract_root)
G. verify contract_root is recomputed from canonical compiled ProofSpec
H. verify every Evidence object:
   - canonical full evidence bytes
   - content-derived EvidenceID
   - response_hash recomputed from actual payload
   - normalized_payload_hash recomputed
   - exact claim binding
   - collector program/runtime manifest binding
   - timestamp sane + not future-skewed
   - freshness policy
   - required evidence classes/count
   - independence groups/policy
I. build evidence_root using ONE evidence Merkle implementation
J. evaluate frozen judges/gates
K. recompute and compare judge_results_root + gate_results_root
L. verify authority_root and exact proposal/payload constraints for
EFFECT receipts
M. execute frozen transition and compare state_after_root
N. compare all signed roots
O. return TRUE/FALSE/UNKNOWN + detailed checked bitmap.

NO =E2=80=9Cchecked.foo=3Dtrue=E2=80=9D is allowed unless a comparison or c=
ryptographic
validation just happened.

PROOFSPEC COMPILER

Current proofspecs/*.json still contain fake labels such as:
  "sha256:xmr_payment_received_schema"
  "sha256:judgeInvoiceObserved"
  bundle_hash: ""
Those are names wearing hash prefixes, not hashes. Current CI scans
src/, so it misses these.

Restructure:
proofspecs/
  src/*.yaml|json       # human-authored semantic source
  schemas/*.json
  policies/*.rego
  dist/*.json           # generated only
  manifest.json

Build command:
  npm run compile:proofspecs

Compiler must:
- validate source schema
- hash actual claim schema bytes
- hash actual evidence schema bytes
- compile policies
- hash actual compiled program bytes
- hash exact config bytes
- hash lockfile/dependency manifest
- emit immutable ProgramManifest
- compute ContractRoot from generated spec
- reject empty/fake hashes
- write deterministic dist output
- CI recomputes and requires git diff empty.

PROGRAM EXECUTION

Do not rely on arbitrary JS judge functions plus a self-declared sourceHash=
.

Strong production option:
- Open Policy Agent: https://github.com/open-policy-agent/opa
- compile Rego gates/judges to WASM:
    opa build -t wasm -e <entrypoint> policy.rego
- Node runtime can use @open-policy-agent/opa-wasm:
  https://github.com/open-policy-agent/npm-opa-wasm

Pin:
- OPA binary/container digest
- policy source hash
- generated policy.wasm SHA-256
- data/config SHA-256
- OPA version/runtime hash
ContractRoot commits to these.

For very simple equality/freshness rules a tiny internal deterministic
AST interpreter is also acceptable, but it must have one pinned
interpreter bundle and declarative AST. Do not allow caller-supplied
JS.

EVIDENCE TREE
Current src/qp/evidence/merkle.ts is a reasonable private commitment
concept, but Replay V2 ignores it and reimplements another Merkle
algorithm.
Converge one API:
  evidenceLeafHash(canonicalEvidence)
  buildEvidenceMerkleTree()
  generateInclusionProof()
  verifyInclusionProof()
Replay must call it directly.

Public =E2=80=9Cno PII=E2=80=9D claim:
regex scanner is advisory only. It cannot prove absence of PII.
Production invariant should instead be:
- public receipt is constructed by a closed schema allowlist from typed fie=
lds
- raw provider payloads can NEVER be copied to public projection
- property/fuzz tests attempt hostile emails/phones/XMR/SimpleX/token strin=
gs
- scanner is defense-in-depth, not cryptographic truth.

Acceptance:
- invalid signature =3D> FULL fails
- missing trust key =3D> FULL fails
- signed receipt / alternate external ReplayInput substitution impossible
- stale evidence =3D> UNKNOWN/fail per exact spec
- modified evidence bytes =3D> root mismatch
- missing required evidence =3D> cannot TRUE
- wrong collector bundle =3D> cannot TRUE
- independence violation =3D> cannot TRUE
- modified policy.wasm =3D> ContractRoot mismatch
- wrong authority =3D> effect cannot TRUE
- state root mutation =3D> replay fail.
